  "Question": "If \\(S=1!+2!+3!+\\cdots+99!,\\) then the units digit in the value of \\(S\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(9\\)",
    "B": "\\(8\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(3\\)",
    "E": "\\(0\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Recall that \\(n!=1\\cdot2\\cdots n\\). For every \\(n\\ge5\\), this product contains both \\(2\\) and \\(5\\), so it contains a factor of \\(10\\) and ends in zero. Adding these terms cannot change the units digit.\n\nWe therefore need only the first four factorials:\n\\[\n1!+2!+3!+4!=1+2+6+24=33.\n\\]\nThe full sum is \\(33\\) plus a multiple of \\(10\\), so its units digit is \\(\\boxed{3}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
